Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Microcassettes Chew the Cold Rail
- Story & Context: In the cramped berth of Nightjet 402 leaving Vienna, audio archivist Julian Cruz accidentally dropped his pocket synth into a half-empty mug of lukewarm, burnt chicory coffee when the train jolted violently over the switchtracks. Singer Eleni Vane caught the sputtering, short-circuited audio loop on her handheld Dictaphone, instantly pitching her voice down an octave to match the rhythmic, low-frequency hum of the car's broken heating vent. Compartment doors rattled open as a furious night conductor threatened to pull the emergency brake, but the duo merely locked eyes and let the pocket-synth kick thud through the vibrating floorboards. Leaning into the condenser capsule, Eleni crooned the bruised refrain that sparked the entire movement: "We don't get sleep, we just trade the rhythm."
