Track 2: "Why Keep the Ruined Minidisc?"
- Story & Context: Stranded on a dead sidetrack outside Innsbruck at 3:00 AM, Eleni sat cross-legged on the scratchy velour seat, peeling decayed adhesive off a cracked ATRAC minidisc containing seven corrupted vocal takes from her former lover. Julian tuned his pocket FM unit to the carriage's emergency frequency, coaxing a hollow, tear-stained 808 kick pattern from the pocket sequencer while the smell of damp winter wool filled the unheated compartment. A sudden burst of suppressed weeping turned into an improvised melisma, blending Nu-Soul micro-runs with the metallic stutter of the disc player's optical laser repeatedly failing to read the table of contents. Through tears that dampened the machine’s tiny silicon keys, she sang into Julian’s overdriven headphone mic: "You loved the playback more than you loved my skin."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Atmospheric lyric video background, a scratched magenta MiniDisc shell sitting atop worn blue passenger seat velour, illuminated by the harsh red glow of an emergency exit sign, reflections of falling snow on train window glass, cinematic shallow depth of field.

Track 3: Eleni’s Descent at Zurich Enge
- Story & Context: By dawn, the rumor of the midnight compartment sessions had already pulled a dozen coat-bundled insomniacs with battery-powered grooveboxes onto Platform 3 of Zurich Enge. As the train’s steel brakes screeched into a final halt and the sharp scent of cold diesel exhaust billowed through the morning mist, Eleni vanished into the commuter crowd, leaving only an unplugged headphone splitter and an alkaline battery leaking on the luggage rack. The remaining commuters kept the master kick drum pounding on their pocket synths in unison, harmonizing their breath in a solemn, soul-stirring chorus that resonated off the station's damp ceramic tiles. The sound engineer who salvaged her abandoned gear swore he heard her recorded voice lingering through the railhead: "Leave the engine running till the ache turns sweet."
